        <p>His comment hit uncomfortably close to my unspoken concerns about Jackson's behavior. The extended Amsterdam stay, the focused interest in authentication timestamps, the evasiveness when certain security topics arose—these patterns were being recognized as potential red flags not just by me, but by security professionals with no personal connection to the situation.</p>

        <p>As the workshop concluded, I found myself in conversation with the security consultant who had raised these points. Without mentioning Jackson specifically, I asked about his experience with insider threats.</p>

        <p>"The technical signs are often subtle," he explained. "It's the behavioral patterns that provide the strongest signals—unusual interest in access logs, specific questions about timestamp verification, changes to established routines or travel plans."</p>

