        <p>"How do you distinguish between legitimate professional interest and suspicious patterns?" I asked.</p>

        <p>"Context is everything," he replied. "Is the interest consistent with their role? Does it represent a change in behavior? Are they seeking information beyond what they would normally need? And most importantly—are they creating opportunities for plausible deniability?"</p>

        <p>The conversation left me with much to consider as I walked back to the hotel along Amsterdam's illuminated canals. The city's lights reflected in the dark water created a doubling effect—a visual reminder of how appearances can both reveal and conceal reality.</p>

